test.yaml:17:29: untrusted input from the variable BODY (github.event.comment.body) is written to $GITHUB_OUTPUT as the record "body=..." and can hold a line break: an attacker who controls it ends the record and adds others, so it sets the other outputs of the step (steps.record.outputs.*) that later steps trust. write a value without line breaks (validate it, or cut it down with tr -d '\n'), or write it between a delimiter that nobody can guess (delimiter=$(uuidgen); echo "body<<$delimiter" ...; echo "$delimiter") [output-clobbering]
test.yaml:27:13: untrusted input from the variable BODY (github.event.comment.body) is written to $GITHUB_OUTPUT between the delimiter "EOF", which is a constant, so the value can hold a line with the delimiter and then any other record: an attacker who controls it sets the other outputs of the step (steps.delimiter.outputs.*) that later steps trust. a constant delimiter is not a fix. use a delimiter that nobody can guess (delimiter=$(uuidgen); echo "body<<$delimiter" ...; echo "$delimiter") or write a value without line breaks [output-clobbering]
test.yaml:32:21: untrusted input from the variable BODY (github.event.comment.body) is written to $GITHUB_OUTPUT as the record "body=..." and can hold a line break: an attacker who controls it ends the record and adds others, so it sets the other outputs of the step (steps.heredoc.outputs.*) that later steps trust. write a value without line breaks (validate it, or cut it down with tr -d '\n'), or write it between a delimiter that nobody can guess (delimiter=$(uuidgen); echo "body<<$delimiter" ...; echo "$delimiter") [output-clobbering]
